  <!-- The mockup's "Reconnect now" action (ADR 0007 §2). A Method, not a
       writable parameter: it has no value to hold, it acts on the live TCP
       connection, and it is gated by the OPC UA Call permission
       (PermissionType.Call, Part 3 §8.55,
       https://reference.opcfoundation.org/Core/Part3/v105/docs/8.55) rather
       than by the parameter form's Write gate — which is the whole reason it
       could not be modelled as a Boolean somebody writes true to.

       It belongs on the LINK for the same reason the diagnostics above do:
       reconnecting is an act on the TCP connection, and several devices share
       one. A per-device Reconnect would give every device on a link the power
       to drop the link out from under its siblings while looking like a
       device-local action.

       No InputArguments/OutputArguments Properties: both are Optional for a
       Method (Part 3 §5.7.1,
       https://reference.opcfoundation.org/Core/Part3/v105/docs/5.7), the link
       knows which connections it holds, and the outcome is the link state the
       rows above already report.

       NOT A STANDARD METHOD, checked rather than assumed. The core spec's only
       comparable surface is PubSubStatusType's Enable/Disable pair over a
       named state machine (Part 14 §9.1.10 / §6.2.1); Reconnect is not a
       transition into a named state but a cycle of the current one, so that
       pattern does not fit. The Devices companion spec (Part 100 §5) models
       ConnectionPointType and NetworkType with no Methods at all, so there is
       nothing to inherit there either. What IS standard and is used: the
       Method node class itself, the Call service (Part 4 §5.11.2,
       https://reference.opcfoundation.org/Core/Part4/v105/docs/5.11.2), the
       Call permission above, and Executable/UserExecutable — which is how a
       client is meant to learn it may not call this, instead of inventing a
       client-side rule. -->
  <UAMethod NodeId="ns=1;i=471" BrowseName="Reconnect" SymbolicName="Iec60870LinkType_Reconnect" ParentNodeId="ns=1;i=124">
    <DisplayName Locale="ru">Переподключить</DisplayName>
    <DisplayName Locale="en">Reconnect</DisplayName>
    <Description>Drops the link&apos;s current connections so it redials immediately. Returns as soon as the close is under way; watch LinkState and LastConnected for the result.</Description>
    <References>
      <Reference ReferenceType="HasComponent" IsForward="false">ns=1;i=124</Reference>
      <Reference ReferenceType="HasModellingRule">i=78</Reference>
    </References>
  </UAMethod>
